45 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500245 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500245 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500245 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500245 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500245 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500245 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186499656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500245 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a1c71d8a-386f-50b9-abbf-82d82b82978a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500250 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500250 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499784 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500250 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500250 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500250 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500250 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500250 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500250 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186499798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500250 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a6b72617-42bc-5f67-b04d-32f60467b95a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500272 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500272 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500272 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500272 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500272 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500272 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500272 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500272 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186500029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500272 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e3ca3a19-dcd8-503a-aaa3-09d81f94236f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500327 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500327 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163218" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500327 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500327 #edb/ref 1071 "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}$\nand has mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{9}xy,$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. The moment of inertia of the plate about a line $l$ perpendicular to the plate is $\\frac{13}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nGiven that the center of mass of the plate is at $(2,2),$ find the distance of the line $l$ from the center of mass." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500327 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "92c86cbd-ae23-56f6-b895-3b862f7ae3ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500327 #edb/ref 1074 "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{9}xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass $(2,2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{―}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}((x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}((x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}x(x-2)^{2}y+x{y}^{3}-4x{y}^{2}+4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{2}x(x-2)^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}x{y}^{4}-\\frac{4}{3}x{y}^{3}+2x{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{9}{4}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{4}-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{9}{8}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{8}-18+\\frac{81}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ \\frac{13}{4} & =\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{9}{4}{d}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{9}{4}{d}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ d & =\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500335 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500335 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164134" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500335 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500335 #edb/ref 1071 "A circular plate of mass $4\\,\\text{kg}$ with uniform mass density occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{m}$ and is centered at the origin.\nGiven that the moment of inertia of the plate about a line $l$ perpendicular to the plate is $56\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ find the distance of the line $l$ from the center of mass of $D.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500335 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a2307504-4cd4-513c-adab-5cca7db9b497" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500335 #edb/ref 1074 "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{10},\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the circular plate $D$ is $A=\\pi \\cdot (\\sqrt{10})^{2}=10\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{4}{10\\pi }=\\frac{2}{5\\pi }\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid $(0,0).$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{10}}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{10}}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5\\pi }\\cdot 25\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =20\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ 56 & =20+4{d}^{2} \\\\ 4{d}^{2} & =36 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =9 \\\\ d & =3\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500372 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500372 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163813" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500372 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500372 #edb/ref 1071 "A circular plate of mass $6\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $3\\,\\text{m}$ centered at the origin.\nFind the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $1\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500372 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ea1b0433-500d-513e-b462-b96776148bf3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500372 #edb/ref 1074 "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 3,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the circular plate $D$ is $A=\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}=9\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{6}{9\\pi }=\\frac{2}{3\\pi }\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid $(0,0).$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{0}^{3}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{81}{4}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =27\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $1\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =27+{1}^{2}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =27+6 \\\\  & =33\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500385 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186500416 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500385 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "04477c12-4f2b-5395-8bf0-f85ecfa83b11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500385 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186500327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500403 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4c0fd999-e432-5b94-beeb-049c81838f59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500403 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186500335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500404 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186500424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500404 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4c58d4a3-e259-5a64-bfb1-3db86ff23f95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500404 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500416 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186500403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500416 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "77423ec6-ca1b-55bf-9ea0-99d7b8c830db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500416 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186500372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500424 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186500385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500424 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9445c9d9-c20e-5877-b779-cef068cded52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500424 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129548 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
